                    "message": "> where did this number 32 come from?\n> \n> while wikipedia mentions min 32 unit loads in the rs485 articile, the list of network busses notes upto 256 and Modbus assigns unit address 1-247 for servers (only one client)\n\n\n32 is without repeaters. I have updated wording to reflect that.\n\n> \n> is this just \"a number at which it should be efficent\"?\n\nRefer to \"Efficient Modbus Access\" section.\n\n> \n> (the limit would seem to be depend on the baud rate achieved, and the 3.5 character gap between rtu messages.)"
